# Line endings are decided here rather than by whatever core.autocrlf happens
# to be set to on the machine doing the commit.
#
# Why this file exists: index.html has been stored with CRLF for its whole
# history, but only by accident. A stray lone CR sat inside one of the workout
# templates, and git skips autocrlf normalisation on content with irregular
# line endings - so that single byte was the only thing keeping the file out of
# the normaliser. Tidying it up let git normalise the whole file, and a commit
# that moved two blocks reported all 2,987 lines as changed. Three separate
# commits in one day had already been mangled this way before the cause was
# found.
#
# index.html is therefore left alone entirely: -text means no conversion in
# either direction, so the bytes on disk are the bytes in the object store and
# no config on any machine can rewrite them. The trade is that git will not
# repair it either, so keep editing it on Windows.
#
# Everything else has always been stored LF and is left to normalise the usual
# way: LF in the repository, native endings in the working tree.

* text=auto

index.html -text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ico binary
